        "text": "Under Article 124 of the 2015 Civil Procedure Code, the Court may freeze an account where there are grounds to establish that the obligor holds that account and freezing is necessary for the resolution of the case or to secure judgment enforcement. The order must correctly identify the account holder, the bank and the scope of the freeze. The bank acts pursuant to a lawful court order, not a creditor’s unilateral request."
