        "text": "Under Articles 111, 124–126 and 133 of the 2015 Civil Procedure Code and Resolution No. 02/2020/NQ-HĐTP, the Court considers: (i) the grounds for and necessity of the particular measure; (ii) the relevant party, assets and scope of the obligation; (iii) evidence supporting the request; (iv) circumstances in which the law does not permit the measure; and (v) security to be provided, where mandatory. Not every request requires proof that the opposing party has already dissipated all its assets, but mere speculation is insufficient."
