        "text": "Not all provisional emergency measures require security. Under Clause 1, Article 136 of the 2015 Civil Procedure Code, applicants seeking the measures in Clauses 6, 7, 8, 10, 11, 15 and 16 of Article 114 must submit documentary evidence of a guarantee secured by assets as prescribed by law, or deposit money, precious metals, gemstones or valuable papers in an amount determined by the Court. Accordingly, the obligation should not invariably be described as a cash deposit."
